*
*
*         Name: errno.en_US.msgs
*               XMITMSGX message repository for ERRNO set in US English
*       Author: Rick Troth, rogue programmer
*         Date: 2017-Dec-01 (Fri)
*
* These messages were initially gathered from C headers on Linux,
* which in turn includes C headers from GLIBC and other packages.
* Additional messages gathered from C headers included with CYGWIN.
*
* The next line sets the token introducer.
& 3
* It also indicates default number of digits, which we ignore.
*
*nnnffllv mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm...
* We don't implement format numbers (ff) or line numbers (ll) but leave
* those columns in this file for compatibility with the CMS impmenentation.
0001    E EPERM, operation not permitted
0002    E ENOENT, no such file or directory &1
0003    E ESRCH, no such process
0004    E EINTR, interrupted system call
0005    E EIO, input/output error
0006    E ENXIO, no such device or address or device not configured
0007    E E2BIG, argument list too long
0008    E ENOEXEC, executable file format error
0009    E EBADF, bad file number or bad file descriptor
0010    E ECHILD, no child processes
0011    E EAGAIN, try the operation again, aka EWOULDBLOCK, the operation would block
* 11    E EAGAIN  No more processes                                       CYG
* 11    E EAGAIN  Resource temporarily unavailable                        SOL
0012    E ENOMEM, not enough memory
0013    E EACCES, permission denied
0014    E EFAULT, bad address or memory segmentation fault
0015    E ENOTBLK, block device required
0016    E EBUSY, device or resource busy
0017    E EEXIST, file exists
0018    E EXDEV, cross-device link
0019    E ENODEV, no such device or operation not supported by device
0020    E ENOTDIR, argument is not a directory
0021    E EISDIR, argument is a directory and should not be
0022    E EINVAL, invalid parameter or argument
0023    E ENFILE, file table overflow, too many open files in system
0024    E EMFILE, too many open files in the system
0025    E ENOTTY, not a character device (historically, not a typewriter)
0026    E ETXTBSY, text file busy
0027    E EFBIG, file too large
0028    E ENOSPC, no space left on device
0029    E ESPIPE, illegal seek
0030    E EROFS, read-only file system
0031    E EMLINK, too many links
0032    E EPIPE, broken pipe
0033    E EDOM, mathematics argument out of domain of function
0034    E ERANGE, result too large, math result not representable
*
* numeric values vary below
0035    E EDEADLK, resource deadlock would occur; aka EDEADLOCK
0036    E ENAMETOOLONG, file name or path name too long
0037    E ENOLCK, no record locks available
0038    E ENOSYS, function not implemented or invalid system call number
0039    E ENOTEMPTY, directory not empty
0040    E ELOOP, too many symbolik links encountered
0041    E ELNRNG, link number out of range
0042    E ENOMSG, no message of desired type
0043    E EIDRM, identifier removed
0044    E ECHRNG, channel number out of range
0045    E EL2NSYNC, level 2 not synchronized
0046    E EL3HLT, level 3 halted
0047    E EL3RST, level 3 reset
0048    E ELNRNG, link number out of range
0049    E EUNATCH, protocol driver not attached
0050    E ENOCSI, no CSI structure available
0051    E EL2HLT, level 2 halted
0052    E EBADE, invalid exchange
0053    E EBADR, invalid request descriptor
0054    E EXFULL, exchange full
0055    E ENOANO, no anode
0056    E EBADRQC, invalid request code
0057    E EBADSLT, invalid slot
* 58    I no error
0059    E EBFONT, bad font file format
0060    E ENOSTR, device or file is not a stream
0061    E ENODATA, no data available (for no delay I/O)
0062    E ETIME, timer expired or stream ioctl timeout
0063    E ENOSR, out of stream resources
0064    E ENONET, this machine is not on the network
0065    E ENOPKG, package not installed
0066    E EREMOTE, the object is remote or too many levels of remote in path
0067    E ENOLINK, the virtual circuit link has been severed
0068    E EADV, advertise error
0069    E ESRMNT, srmount error
0070    E ECOMM, communication error on send
0071    E EPROTO, protocol error
0072    E EMULTIHOP, multihop attempted
0073    I EDOTDOT, RFS specific error or cross mount point
0074    E EBADMSG, not a data message
0075    E EOVERFLOW, value too large for defined data type
0076    E ENOTUNIQ, name not unique on network
0077    E EBADFD, file descriptor &1 is in a bad state or invalid for this operation
0078    E EREMCHG, remote address changed
0079    E ELIBACC, cannot access a needed shared library
0080    E ELIBBAD, accessing corrupted shared library %1
0081    E ELIBSCN, .lib section in a.out is corrupted
0082    E ELIBMAX, attempting to link in too many shared libraries
0083    E ELIBEXEC, cannot exec a shared library directly
0084    E EILSEQ, illegal byte sequence
0085    E ERESTART, interrupted system call should be restarted
0086    E ESTRPIPE, streams pipe error
0087    E EUSERS, too many users
0088    E ENOTSOCK, attempted socket operation on non-socket
0089    E EDESTADDRREQ, destination address required
0090    E EMSGSIZE, message too long
0091    E EPROTOTYPE, protocol is wrong type for socket
0092    E ENOPROTOOPT, protocol not available
0093    E EPROTONOSUPPORT, protocol not supported
0094    E ESOCKTNOSUPPORT, socket type not supported
